NAME
    man - display the detailed manual page for a command or topic

SYNOPSIS
    man <topic>
    man

DESCRIPTION
    man shows the in-system manual page for a TOS command or concept. It sits
    between 'help' and the external Manual in depth:

        help    quick, get-you-going, and shows only what's installed here
        man     detailed per-topic pages (this command)
        MANUAL  the full external book (MANUAL.md), for the deepest reference

    With no argument, man lists the pages available on this machine. Pages live
    under /usr/man/ as plain text; packages may install their own.

    Under the panels TUI a page opens in a scrollable view tab; in the CLI shell
    it prints to the screen.

EXAMPLES
    man             List every installed manual page.
    man pkg         Read the package-manager page.
    man networking  Read the networking concepts page.

SEE ALSO
    help, help <command>, MANUAL.md
